---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { config } from '../lib/config';
---

<Layout
  title="Terms"
  description="Practical terms for using Makeatimer’s free browser timers and calculations."
  path="/terms/"
>
  <article class="prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">Updated September 29, 2026</p>
    <h1>Terms of use</h1>
    <p>
      Makeatimer is a free browser tool operated by {config.operator}.
      Questions: <a href={`mailto:${config.email}`}>{config.email}</a>.{' '}
      <a href="https://faxcorp.dev/company/">Company details</a>.
    </p>
    <h2>Using the results</h2>
    <p>
      Check important results independently. Calculations depend on your inputs,
      displayed rounding, browser support, and time-zone data. Work-hour tools
      calculate time and do not determine legal payroll or overtime obligations.
      Speech and render tools are estimates based on the assumptions shown.
    </p>
    <h2>Timer availability</h2>
    <p>
      Browser alarms require an available browser. Closing a tab, suspending a
      device, changing the device clock, or restricting background activity can
      delay or prevent an alarm. Use a suitable independent alarm for anything
      requiring guaranteed timing.
    </p>
    <h2>Availability and changes</h2>
    <p>
      We may update the tools or interrupt availability for maintenance. The
      service is provided as available. These terms do not limit rights that
      applicable law makes mandatory.
    </p>
    <h2>Source license</h2>
    <p>
      The application source is provided under the MIT license. That source
      license is separate from these website usage terms.
    </p>
  </article>
</Layout>
